; Harvester5Pip -- AGGRESSIVE SCALPING preset, M1 variant
; Attach to EUR/USD, timeframe M1.
;
; Same geometry as aggressive_M5.set. Only the timeframe changes, which changes
; what the indicators actually see:
;
;   SMA(20)/ATR(20)/ER(20) on M1 span 20 MINUTES, versus 100 min on M5 and
;   300 min on M15. The anchor therefore tracks microstructure noise rather
;   than any usable local mean, and ATR(20) on M1 EUR/USD is typically 1-2
;   pips -- so with ATRMult 1.0 spacing is pinned at the 2.5p floor
;   permanently and volatility adaptation is entirely OFF.
;
; Windows are lengthened 3x (20 -> 60) so they span a comparable WALL-CLOCK
; period to the M5 preset. Without this, "M1 vs M5" is not a timeframe test,
; it is an accidental indicator-period test and the results are not comparable.
;
; Tester requirement: M1 results are extremely sensitive to tick quality.
; Use "Every tick based on real ticks" or the fill counts are fiction.
;
; Magic 770503 -- MUST differ from the other two presets.
;
InpTPPips=2.5
InpLotsPerLevel=0.02
InpATRMult=1.0
InpSpacingMinPips=2.5
InpSpacingMaxPips=6.0
InpWiden=0.25
InpMaxLevels=3
InpPrePlaceLevels=2
InpReanchorMult=3.0
InpBasketMult=6.0
InpEquityStopPct=6.0
InpDisasterMult=2.0
InpCooldownBars=1440
InpCooldownMins=1440
InpAnchorMA=60
InpATRPeriod=60
InpERWindow=60
InpERFull=0.35
InpERHalf=0.50
InpRSIPeriod=42
InpRSILongVeto=25.0
InpRSIShortVeto=75.0
InpBWExpansionMult=1.6
InpBWMedianBars=150
InpRolloverMins=5
InpFlatOnFriday=true
InpFridayCloseHour=20
InpMagic=770503
InpSlippagePoints=10
InpVerboseLog=true
InpCsvLog=true
InpCsvCommonFolder=false
